{
  "slug": "claude-security",
  "name": "Claude Security",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Find and fix vulnerabilities before attackers exploit them. A team of agents maps your code, hunts for exploitable flaws and challenges every finding, so you spend your time on real bugs. Get patches analyzed by a panel of agents, and apply them when you choose. Triage other scanners' results, build a threat model, review pull requests with a GitHub Action, and see your hosted Claude Security findings.",
  "longDescription": "Runs a security review as a team of agents inside your session: map the architecture, build a threat model, hunt each component, and independently verify every finding before it is reported — then turn confirmed findings into patch files you review and apply yourself.\n\n- **Scan codebase**: the whole repository or a scoped part of it\n- **Scan changes**: a branch's, pull request's or single commit's diff\n- **Suggest patches**: a report's findings as targeted patch files\n\nStart from the `/claude-security` menu. Scans run in your session under your permissions — scan untrusted third-party code inside a sandbox.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 6,
    "agent": 17,
    "hook": 5
  },
  "sourceType": "official",
  "author": {
    "name": "Anthropic"
  },
